\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces From interaction to targeted training and transfer. Top: A asks B to help repair a bridge while M observes; M infers A's preference, considers its own, and proposes collaboration to A. Bottom left: colored nodes and paths select game slices, which the oracle solves. Bottom center: direct current-state-to-action supervision (O) is augmented with separately generated inference and planning labels (D) for GRPO training. Bottom right: in the CalBench transfer setting, M coordinates a meeting using its private calendar and partners' replies.}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:overview}{{1}{2}{From interaction to targeted training and transfer. Top: A asks B to help repair a bridge while M observes; M infers A's preference, considers its own, and proposes collaboration to A. Bottom left: colored nodes and paths select game slices, which the oracle solves. Bottom center: direct current-state-to-action supervision (O) is augmented with separately generated inference and planning labels (D) for GRPO training. Bottom right: in the CalBench transfer setting, M coordinates a meeting using its private calendar and partners' replies}{figure.1}{}}
